  "planning_notes": [
    "Board is Arduino Uno (arduino:avr:uno). Exact pin assignments preserved: D2/D3/D4 are the three bed call inputs; D7 is nurse confirm; D13 is LED output; D6 is buzzer tone output; TM1637 uses CLK=D8 and DIO=D5.",
    "All ports for the explicitly wired functional pins are represented: D2, D3, D4, D7, D13, D6, D8, D5.",
    "No explicit pullup/active polarity was provided for buttons; digital_input requests use no pullup/active_high override, so the model must handle electrical polarity via active_high if required.",
    "The 10ms control_period_ms is a scheduling granularity; debouncing, call-priority ordering, wait-time accumulation, and log/serial cadence belong in the SysML model.",
    "TM1637 'tm1637_number' is used to display the combined 'bed ID and waiting seconds' according to model logic (selection/count formatting handled by SysML). The initial display command is 0 and leading_zero is false.",
    "Tone duration/pauses and buzzer behavior are implemented in the model using elapsed_ms; the tone_output port is initialized to silence (0).",
    "Serial reporting uses one numeric group gated by a Boolean trigger output; exact message contents/formatting and when to report are model-managed (fixed text lines were not explicitly required, so only typed numeric values are defined)."
  ],
